n": "The gist is to make color organize the drawing."}, {"id": "fe19ba6a-02a8-496d-a28d-73ecaea84bff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mood and meaning", "children": [{"id": "0ab0225a-22a7-4134-a587-09f10c5305f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Atmosphere, symbolic color, memory, identity, and narrative tone"}, {"id": "2a6eef7a-b671-4bd0-ae22-45a433ea47a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Restraint and palette design"}, {"id": "2dfadad8-a8aa-4b5c-9abc-0f24835ac5e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Color critique vocabulary"}], "description": "Students use color to shape emotional and conceptual effect."}]}, {"id": "62543a00-5180-4051-85e6-7bd4d6ec028d", "type": "topic", "title": "Figure Drawing from Life: Gesture, Proportion, Movement, Structure, and Presence", "description": "Students develop a responsive figure-drawing practice rooted in looking, time, anatomy, movement, and embodied presence.", "children": [{"id": "77fc0978-6176-4740-9c37-afea91686806", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gesture and pose", "children": [{"id": "aca9b4cb-3694-40e2-91fe-e9b6a3d619af", "type": "concept", "title": "Line of action, weight, balance, rhythm, and timed poses"}, {"id": "06c5196c-20a6-4bdc-a27b-3e2233948d40", "type": "concept", "title": "Short pose to long pose development"}, {"id": "111f0e49-d94c-4c3d-bee1-ee72466a2b9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Movement and compression"}], "description": "Students learn to capture the living action of the figure."}, {"id": "2277a7da-f135-42dd-8d84-a53deabd9444", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Proportion and structure", "children": [{"id": "1403662e-6bdb-4a36-a63b-b411df54f015", "type": "concept", "title": "Head units, landmarks, torso masses, pelvis, limbs, hands, feet, and head structure"}, {"id": "143df263-d9e2-4e2d-a5f1-3cbfcb7af184", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreshortening and proportional correction"}, {"id": "063331ec-deb0-49e5-8ef1-6c30744322e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Structure without stiffness"}], "description": "The point is to balance observation with anatomical scaffolding."}, {"id": "68d06756-7d2c-46f3-a5f5-39475c773a33", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presence and expression", "children": [{"id": "b25fd553-b71f-45bd-ae5e-2e435c9d5152", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity, posture, vulnerability, consent, gaze, and respect"}, {"id": "781143e3-2be2-4007-a95d-1cf9374125dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Model etiquette and studio professionalism"}, {"id": "2bdd23ee-0bc5-473a-a7ea-62b1cb4fe87d", "type": "concept", "title": "Figure as subject, form, and relation"}], "description": "Students consider figure drawing as more than anatomy exercise."}]}, {"id": "2955f2ac-7553-4911-b199-de828880c604", "type": "topic", "title": "Anatomy for Artists: Skeleton, Muscles, Planes, Landmarks, Hands, Feet, and Portrait Structure", "description": "This topic gives students structural knowledge that supports expressive and accurate figure work.", "children": [{"id": "ca731f87-43db-4fe1-aed5-a903b6534284", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Skeletal landmarks", "children": [{"id": "0aa7708c-6da0-4341-83b8-78dcbff78319", "type": "concept", "title": "Skull, spine, rib cage, pelvis, scapula, clavicle, joints, and major bony landmarks"}, {"id": "51f3a0e7-1092-4fe3-a92d-18ef9040a2a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Balance, tilt, and alignment"}, {"id": "d4d87cf1-4c41-4152-80b9-303c333a19de", "type": "concept", "title": "Anatomy visible on the surface"}], "description": "Students learn the durable structure under surface form."}, {"id": "ac29f2a5-218b-498b-8a33-4c85487152be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Muscle groups and planes", "children": [{"id": "e050c8b8-2a6a-499f-8c09-ddde3c0b2495", "type": "concept", "title": "Torso, shoulder, arm, leg, neck, face, and back muscle groups"}, {"id": "fc941a2c-5dc4-447b-82f5-43473055eb5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Planes, masses, tendons, and compression"}, {"id": "078624c0-e29c-4525-90a0-b90d79f16b79", "type": "concept", "title": "Anatomy for movement and weight"}], "description": "The gist is to simplify anatomy into usable drawing knowledge."}, {"id": "1aa43608-ee7e-4cef-9e16-df0281bc8d4a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hands, feet, and portrait", "children": [{"id": "9558b344-6ab0-4847-8817-d94082681bff", "type": "concept", "title": "Hand construction, foot construction, head planes, features, and expression"}, {"id": "f5c94cf0-ff10-4ec6-a4d9-bf024cd1d4ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture and proportion in extremities"}, {"id": "fb274237-129e-4eee-be9e-aadaec06818a", "type": "concept", "title": "Common distortions and corrections"}], "description": "Students focus on forms that often reveal weak structure."}]}, {"id": "5d460b73-cdb0-406f-8e91-d8fb6abf8389", "type": "topic", "title": "Drawing from Memory, Body, Movement, Score, Diagram, and Performance", "description": "Students move beyond direct observation into drawing as memory, notation, action, instruction, and performative trace.", "children": [{"id": "d9b54cae-a103-4759-b811-58b31ea67b77", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Memory drawing", "children": [{"id": "3dc3a99c-27f1-43c7-bbf6-935d9ced88c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Memory maps, emotional space, dream imagery, and reconstructed scenes"}, {"id": "1aaf4870-2ac5-416b-8dab-3af5bb256946", "type": "concept", "title": "Distortion as meaning"}, {"id": "aac42261-19f9-4a12-8c87-98bdd1e3e82c", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation stored in the body"}], "description": "Students draw from remembered experience rather than direct sight."}, {"id": "6180e576-98fc-4b00-bf05-36e7c9a2c25c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Body and movement", "children": [{"id": "1c3a8049-2213-424d-a2eb-85a0e163fb8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Walking lines, breath marks, repetitive motions, dance, reach, and pressure"}, {"id": "9a1027f8-b2b4-4a86-b6d3-08494926ef66", "type": "concept", "title": "Drawing tools attached to body movement"}, {"id": "fe86e96e-d9b9-4e71-9ec8-0a9e0d8d0b8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Process documentation"}], "descrip