gist is to generate work through chosen limits."}, {"id": "f453405d-0e2a-4cd8-a359-ecde29e5de09", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research-based drawing", "children": [{"id": "bb8c8769-3c0d-4857-a1a5-fa9ba2c42380", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist research, historical images, field notes, interviews, objects, and archives"}, {"id": "affb31be-e6d1-4882-ad0a-0539c2ec3a70", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation and source transformation"}, {"id": "98a77a6f-065d-4f53-8499-2f919132e66c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics of borrowed material"}], "description": "Students connect drawing to external inquiry."}]}, {"id": "16128667-bc2c-4d98-b995-265ba85cc86c", "type": "topic", "title": "Drawing as Final Work: Composition, Series, Editing, Scale, Craft, and Exhibition", "description": "Students learn how drawings become finished works through sustained decisions about composition, material, sequence, and presentation.", "children": [{"id": "be676084-5dbd-4b05-9dbd-4c3e293c5b6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Composition and resolution", "children": [{"id": "a3c54452-c5ec-405f-bef5-601e4ef29149", "type": "concept", "title": "Balance, emphasis, rhythm, edge, tension, silence, density, and focal structure"}, {"id": "8ea29c51-d48a-4160-81c5-01c2b366faab", "type": "concept", "title": "Resolution versus overworking"}, {"id": "a53f5036-b438-4536-81d6-2ee1667af448", "type": "concept", "title": "Criteria for completion"}], "description": "Students learn how a drawing becomes finished."}, {"id": "e6922231-f95e-4662-b86c-fb4d0505f9a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editing and sequence", "children": [{"id": "b93bc342-7796-493a-abec-2a7c986e28c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Rejects, studies, variations, groupings, order, and pacing"}, {"id": "9fcac874-46b5-431d-aa56-69cf7411e923", "type": "concept", "title": "Diptych, triptych, grid, wall sequence, and book format"}, {"id": "450501d0-b771-4d66-9f5a-3de9e2d7730e", "type": "concept", "title": "Series logic"}], "description": "The point is to make drawings stronger through selection."}, {"id": "7ec86576-dcc2-4315-887a-e0fb62aeb1e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation craft", "children": [{"id": "7ecb4a79-7483-4ffc-9ebe-79a8b8eba41a", "type": "concept", "title": "Mounting, matting, pinning, framing, storage, labeling, and lighting"}, {"id": "f0876a1a-b3f7-4783-8e2d-94087b46afde", "type": "concept", "title": "Surface protection and documentation"}, {"id": "1c5c83ab-1a5f-48fa-8d87-1d2e16bf201c", "type": "concept", "title": "Exhibition decisions"}], "description": "Students learn to care for the physical life of the drawing."}]}, {"id": "9c7e852b-a296-4f3f-bea3-7cfa70b897be", "type": "topic", "title": "Contemporary Drawing Practices: Abstraction, Identity, Feminist Art, Global Context, and Expanded Media", "description": "This topic places student work within modern and contemporary drawing practices across media, movements, identities, and global contexts.", "children": [{"id": "355a9fda-c6cd-419e-8dc0-286a057773e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modern and contemporary contexts", "children": [{"id": "1a7621e2-9932-4a5b-a842-781a7d0948e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Cubism, abstraction, Surrealism, Abstract Expressionism, Minimalism, Conceptual Art, and contemporary practice"}, {"id": "9e69f5b3-ba47-4e9d-a039-fce3eec0486f", "type": "concept", "title": "Drawing after photography and digital media"}, {"id": "3b051268-de9d-44cb-83e7-1f5760bcd885", "type": "concept", "title": "Drawing as autonomous practice"}], "description": "Students place drawing within broader art histories."}, {"id": "32d290b5-9fca-43a9-be7e-da2196e7ba00", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Identity and politics", "children": [{"id": "2a911654-da89-4fa4-9a7e-6e425475f4c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist art, identity-based art, race, gender, class, diaspora, and body politics"}, {"id": "3eaa4b87-ee0c-4009-aa87-0c58c8678aec", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and self-representation"}, {"id": "e6e5e7d5-f47c-44